	"description": [
		"Through nonfiction, fiction, and poetry, students explore the complex relations between humans and the \"natural\" world. Students consider questions such as the following: What does it mean to be connected to a landscape? What is a sense of place? Students also reflect on how they and the writers they read put landscape into language. Also counts toward environmental studies major (all emphases) and concentration. Prerequisite: WRIT 120 or equivalent."
